            <ArticleTitle>IGF-I deficiency, longevity and cancer protection of patients with Laron syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>123-133</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1383-5742(16)30083-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.mrrev.2016.08.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Laron syndrome (LS) is a unique model of congenital IGF-I deficiency. It is characterized by dwarfism and obesity, and is caused by deletion or mutations of the growth hormone receptor (GH-R) gene. It is hypothesized that LS is an old disease originating in Indonesia and that the mutated gene spread to South Asia, the Middle East, the Mediterranean region and South America.</AbstractText>
